        {
          "id": 2088489701,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "@geraldcombs @AndersBroman On Debian this should be `prefix=${pcfiledir}/../../..` due to the .pc file being installed in a multiarch location.\nThis change breaks building libvirt's externally maintained plugin and I guess any external plugin on Debian/Ubuntu.\nIs there a use case where `DESTDIR` should differ from `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`, i.e. where/when is this change beneficial?\n\nI can patch the .pc.in file on Debian and carry that patch, but reverting this change in `master` and on the 4.4 branch would be a simpler option unless there is a clear benefit in keeping the change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
